Chapter: ScopeRuntimeSpawn
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 A child may not escape its parent's scope by being born.

 The process table already copies the parent's capability MASK into a
 child at spawn, and if the scope did not travel beside it the whole
 ring would have a door in it: a program scoped to "OK" could spawn a
 child whose scope cell was zero, and a zero scope is an unscoped grant
 -- the empty prefix admits every path. The child would inherit the
 authority to touch the disk and lose the limit on what it may name,
 which is a capability amplification dressed as a fork.

 So the parent here is scoped to "OK" and does nothing itself. The child
 attempts BOTH writes and reports both answers in one number: ten if the
 in-scope write landed, plus one if the out-of-scope write landed.

 It has to attempt both, and the reason is the whole discipline of this
 battery. A child that reported only the refusal would print the same
 number whether the scope was inherited or the write was simply broken
 in a spawned process -- a failure that happens for the wrong reason
 looks exactly like a success. Attempting both separates them:

   10  the in-scope write landed and the out-of-scope write was refused.
       Writes work in a child AND the scope came with it. This is the
       only passing answer.
   11  both landed: the child's scope cell was zero, an empty prefix
       admits everything, and the door is open. This is the number the
       test exists to catch.
    0  neither landed: writes do not work in a spawned process at all,
       and a test that only checked the refusal would have called that
       a pass.

 Both effectful calls sit in tail or argument position rather than in a
 let: a let bound to a value with a concrete effect row is CDX2033, and
 poke-byte is itself effectful, so binding the report would be rejected
 before the write ever mattered. Nest, do not bind.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Concurrent, Console, FileSystem.Read "OK", Device.Block] Integer
  opening = act
    pid <- process-spawn (\x -> poke-byte 28000 0 ((if fat16-write-file "OK.TXT" "yes" then 10 else 0) + (if fat16-write-file "NO.TXT" "nope" then 1 else 0)))
    let y = process-yield
    in peek-byte 28000 0
  end
